{
  "about": "The code that carries its hub (FleetCore PairingCode, F7 B3): for a hub at http://<an IPv4 address in 100.64.0.0/10>:8765 the Mac shows 13 characters, AAAAA-CCCC-CCCC: 5 for the address, then the hub's own code of 8, which is what a device sends to POST /ui/owner/enroll. Each character is 5 bits, its place in alphabet. The 5 hold 25 bits, highest first: the 22 bits of the address minus 100.64.0.0, then 3 check bits: the CRC-3 with x^3 + x + 1 (1011) of those 22 bits followed by the 40 bits of the code's 8 characters, each from its highest bit (the remainder of those 62 bits followed by three zeros). Any other hub (another port, a name, https, an address outside the network, a path) keeps the code of 8. A reader drops spaces and hyphens, takes small letters as capitals, refuses any other character, takes 8 characters as a code for the hub that it knows, and 13 as a hub and a code when the check bits match; anything else it refuses before any request.",
